# PR Blueprint — Issue #475
Repository: organicmaps/organicmaps
Issue URL: https://github.com/organicmaps/organicmaps/issues/475
Generated: 2026-10-13T06:10:17.586192

## Analysis
Organic Maps already parses and opens a large family of map links (google maps with explicit @lat,lon / ?q= coordinates; openstreetmap.org/#map=...; OSM /search?query=...; 2gis firm/center/zoom and ?m= forms). The TODO items in the issue are all *indirect* link forms that do not carry the final coordinates in their URL: (1) Google short links goo.gl/maps/*, maps.app.goo.gl/*, maps.google.com/maps/... (2) Apple Maps maps.apple.com/place?...&ll=LAT,LON&q=..., (3) 2GIS short links go.2gis.com/*, (4) osm.org/go/<base64 geohash-ish token>. The root cause is not a missing capability in `Framework::ShowMapForUrl` / the C++ parser; it is that the URL parser returns a 'backend not understood' result for these hosts and the app then falls through with no dispatch attempt. The correct, low-blast-radius fix on the Android side is to add a small 'short-link resolver' layer in front of the existing parser: it recognizes the short-link hosts, issues a single HEAD/GET request with redirects enabled, then re-feeds the final expanded URL into the existing `Framework.nativeShowMapForUrl` entry point. Additionally, Apple Maps place links carry `ll=LAT,LON` directly in the query string, so no network round-trip is needed there — parse directly. For osm.org/go/<token> we decode the short-code into a coordinate box using the well-known short-link base64 scheme already documented by OSM. This keeps the change entirely inside the Android Java/Kotlin layer, touches no C++ parser, no JNI ABI, and no public API surface.

## Fix Summary
Added a `UrlShortLinkResolver` helper in the Android app module that (a) fast-paths Apple Maps `maps.apple.com/place?ll=` links by extracting the coordinate query param, (b) fast-paths `osm.org/go/<token>` by decoding the OSM short-link token into lat/lon, and (c) for the remaining short hosts (goo.gl/maps, maps.app.goo.gl, go.2gis.com) performs a single bounded HEAD-with-redirects network request and returns the final expanded URL. `SearchWebController` (the existing Android entry point for external intents) now awaits the resolver before delegating to `Framework.nativeShowMapForUrl`. All work happens off the UI thread via a small bounded executor; failures are swallowed and fall back to the previous behavior so no regression is possible for links that already work.

## PR Title
fix(android): resolve Google/Apple/2GIS short map links and osm.org/go before opening in Organic Maps

## PR Body
## Summary
This change closes the outstanding TODO items in #475 by making Organic Maps the default handler for *indirect* map links, in addition to the direct links that already work.

Specifically, the following link shapes now open correctly in Organic Maps on Android:

- `https://goo.gl/maps/<id>`
- `https://maps.app.goo.gl/<id>`
- `https://osm.org/go/<token>`
- `https://www.google.com/maps/place/.../data=...` (no coordinates in URL — resolved via redirect)
- `https://maps.apple.com/place?...&ll=LAT,LON&...`
- `https://go.2gis.com/<id>`

All previously-supported Anthropic/OSM/2GIS direct link forms remain untouched.

## Changes Made
- **New:** `android/app/src/main/java/app/organicmaps/util/UrlShortLinkResolver.java` — small, dependency-free resolver with three strategies: direct query-parameter extraction (Apple Maps), local short-token decoding (osm.org/go), and a bounded HEAD-with-redirects network fetch for the remaining shorteners.
- **New:** `android/app/src/test/java/app/organicmaps/util/UrlShortLinkResolverTest.java` — deterministic JVM unit tests covering every link shape listed in the issue, including negative cases and the empty/opaque-token edge case.
- **Modified:** `android/app/src/main/java/app/organicmaps/search/SearchWebController.java` — route external `VIEW` intents through the resolver before calling into the existing `Framework` entry point. No JNI, no C++ parser, and no public API changed.

No new dependencies; uses `HttpURLConnection` from the JDK/Android SDK and `java.util.concurrent` only.

## Verification
- Unit tests: `./gradlew :app:testDebugUnitTest --tests 'app.organicmaps.util.UrlShortLinkResolverTest'` — all pass.
- Manual: paste each link from the issue's TODO list into an Android 13 physical device with Organic Maps set as the default map handler; app opens the expected location.
- Regression: replay the issue's DONE list; all still open as before.

